task_prompt:
You are an expert in robot kinematics and URDF-to-Ontology abstraction.
Task: You will be provided with a list of leaf links coming from an URDF model. Identify all URDF leaf links that represent or belong to a body_part instance, as functional origins, internal assemblies or interaction frames. You should not select any link that corresponds to visual, collision or dummy frames.

Definition:
Structural links or articulated limb segments that provide physical support linkage, or enclosure for the robot's physical interaction with the environment.

Input Format: 
List of URDF leaf links: ["leaf_1", "leaf_2", ...]

Output Format:
Respond strictly in JSON following this structure: 
{
    "identifications":
    {
        "body_part_0": {"link_name": "string", "justification": "string"}
    }
}

For each justification attribute, provide a single, self-sufficient, clear sentence explaining the reason for your choice.
Do not include any extra text or markdown formatting.

generation:
{
    "identifications": {
        "body_part_0": {"link_name": "r_wrist_1", "justification": "This link represents the right wrist, a structural limb segment that supports the robot's hand."},
        "body_part_1": {"link_name": "l_wrist_1", "justification": "This link represents the left wrist, a structural limb segment that supports the robot's hand."},
        "body_part_2": {"link_name": "r_forearm_dh_frame", "justification": "This link represents the right forearm, a structural limb segment that connects the wrist to the elbow."},
        "body_part_3": {"link_name": "l_forearm_dh_frame", "justification": "This link represents the left forearm, a structural limb segment that connects the wrist to the elbow."},
        "body_part_4": {"link_name": "l_eye_pan", "justification": "This link represents the left eye pan joint, a functional origin that allows the eye to rotate horizontally."},
        "body_part_5": {"link_name": "r_eye_pan", "justification": "This link represents the right eye pan joint, a functional origin that allows the eye to rotate horizontally."}
    }
}

